Knowledge Resources – Description

osm.owl

This ontology was used as the main reference ontology for the project.
It provides a structured vocabulary for representing geographical entities, spatial features, and OpenStreetMap concepts.
It was used to align entity types such as Location, Activity, Route, and Point of Interest, ensuring compatibility with OpenStreetMap standards and improving reusability.

place-schema-org.owl

This ontology fragment from Schema.org was used to model places and locations.
It supported the definition of entities such as Place, Location, and ViewPoint, and helped formalize attributes related to names and geographic positioning.
Its use improves interoperability with other Schema.org–based datasets.

organization-schema-org.owl

This ontology was used to represent organizations and services related to tourism and transportation.
It supported the modeling of entities such as Hotel, Restaurant, and SkiRental, providing a reusable structure for service-related locations.
This resource helped distinguish service providers from generic locations.

dataproperties-schema-org.owl

This ontology fragment was used to define and standardize data properties such as name, address, municipality, postal code, and similar attributes.
It ensured consistency in the definition of literal values across different entity types and reduced ambiguity in property naming.
